/-! ## Uniform `PK.seed`; deterministic and hedged `opt_rand` -/

/-- **SUF-CMA and EUF-CMA of the byte-level scheme computed by the Rust code, SLH-DSA-SHA2-192f,
internal interface;
uniform `PK.seed`; deterministic signing: `opt_rand = PK.seed` (`sha2RandomizerOfPkSeed` is the identity on
`Bytes 24`, `MReduction.detRand`).**  Instance of `rust_security` (b), (c), which hold for
arbitrary `pkSeedDist` and `optRand`; the bound `Reduction.betaSufFinalMemo` / `betaEufFinalMemo`
at the displayed typed forger is by definition the twelve terms written out in `rust_security`. -/
theorem rust_security_deterministic :
    (∀ F : SignatureAlg.StrongUnforgeableAdversary
        (bytesAlg Sha2Set.s192f.vp Sha2Set.s192f.prims (codec Sha2Set.s192f)
          (fun pk => (pure (sha2RandomizerOfPkSeed Sha2Set.s192f.vp.params pk.pkSeed) : ProbComp Sha2Set.s192f.prims.Y))
          ($ᵗ Sha2Set.s192f.prims.PkSeed)),
      SignatureAlg.strongUnforgeableAdvantage ProbCompRuntime.probComp F ≤
        Reduction.betaSufFinalMemo (bytesToTypedS F).toUnforgeableAdversary) ∧
    ∀ A : SignatureAlg.UnforgeableAdversary
        (bytesAlg Sha2Set.s192f.vp Sha2Set.s192f.prims (codec Sha2Set.s192f)
          (fun pk => (pure (sha2RandomizerOfPkSeed Sha2Set.s192f.vp.params pk.pkSeed) : ProbComp Sha2Set.s192f.prims.Y))
          ($ᵗ Sha2Set.s192f.prims.PkSeed)),
      SignatureAlg.unforgeableAdvantage ProbCompRuntime.probComp A ≤
        Reduction.betaEufFinalMemo (bytesToTyped A) :=
  ⟨fun F => MReduction.slhdsa_sha2_192f_bytes_suf_cma_deterministic F,
    fun A => MReduction.slhdsa_sha2_192f_bytes_euf_cma_deterministic A⟩

/-- **SUF-CMA and EUF-CMA of the byte-level scheme computed by the Rust code, SLH-DSA-SHA2-192f,
